{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `y`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: reordered the two parameter prior sampling statements so that `tau` is observed with its prior before it is used in the hierarchical prior for `theta`. This preserves the same posterior/log density because Stan sampling statements add commutative log-density terms. No data fields were added or changed.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int<lower=0> K;                       // Number of contexts
  int<lower=0> N;                       // Number of observations
  vector[N] y;                          // Observations
  array[N] int<lower=1, upper=K> context_idx; // Context assignments
  real<lower=0> sigma;                  // Measurement variability
}

parameters {
  // Horseshoe parameters
  vector[K] theta;
  real<lower=0> tau;
}

model {
  // Horseshoe prior model
  tau ~ normal(0, 10);
  theta ~ double_exponential(0, tau);

  // Observational model
  y ~ normal(theta[context_idx], sigma);
}
","data_safe_json":"{"K":2,"N":2,"context_idx":[2,2],"sigma":3.7830399471784797,"y":[2.0,2.0]}","protected_variables":["y"]}
